gm-method (eliminate a per-candidate CPU-fractal placement bottleneck while keeping client/server parity): when veg/grass/rock placement calls frame.groundHeightLocal ~1000x/chunk and a profiler shows the CPU fractal (groundHeightLocal/heightAt) is ~half the total time, the fix is NOT to rewrite placement - it's to OVERRIDE frame.groundHeightLocal with an O(1) GPU-patch lookup (bake the patch once off the real shader, bilinear-sample, cache per patch). Because placement reads height ONLY through frame.groundHeightLocal, swapping that one fn makes all placement use the lookup with ZERO placement-code change and preserved determinism. PARITY-SAFE: client + server both override with the SAME shared height-fn over the SAME deterministic GPU bake -> byte-identical placement (the shared placementsForChunk contract holds). KEY: the client builds its OWN SEPARATE OffscreenCanvas baker (independent of the live-render GL) - calling the render context's bake mid-frame contends + returns null. Witness the win by PROFILE (the browser `profile` verb prefix): the fractal fn should DISAPPEAR from the top culprits (was 48% -> absent). The per-patch cache IS the 'batching' (a chunk's ~1000 samples hit one cached patch). Match patch density to the finest display LOD (2R/2^maxLevel / (gridMeshSize-1)) so collision/placement == what's drawn, no reduction.